WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:06.200
Netflix's newest fan favorite is the heartbreaking
13 Reasons Why. A teen drama based on the

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:12.070
2007 Jay Asher novel of the same name, the
series features a ton of fresh-faced actors,

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:16.650
including one you'll swear you've seen before:
Dylan Minnette, who stars as Clay Jensen.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:20.869
Why is he so familiar? Here are thirteen reasons
why ...

00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:22.250
Saving Grace

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:27.800
Minnette first made his mark in 2007 as a
series regular in this TNT crime drama, where

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.870
he played another character named Clay: the
young and oh-so lovable Clay Norman, the nephew

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.429
of the strung-out, self-destructive detective
played by Holly Hunter. Minnette's mature

00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:43.620
performance earned him back-to-back Young
Artist Awards in 2008 and 2009.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.800
Lost

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.339
His next big TV role was short-lived, but
what a role it was: in 2010, Minnette played

00:00:50.339 --> 00:00:54.559
David Shephard, the sort-of son of Jack and
Juliet, on the controversial sixth and final

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:58.250
season of the time-hopping ABC adventure drama
Lost.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:02.629
Fans likely remember Minnette from the episode
"Lighthouse," in which Jack sits David down

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:03.710
for a heart-to-heart …

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:11.980
"I will always love you. No matter what you
do. In my eyes, you can never fail."

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.600
Too bad Minnette's character only existed
in a post-death metaphysical realm ... but

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.920
that's just how Lost rolled.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.350
Let Me In

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.380
Here's where things get dark. Minnette entered
the horror scene that same year as a bully

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:30.910
named Kenny in this adaptation of the 2008
Swedish vampire flick, Let the Right One In.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:32.060
"Hey little girl."

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.840
His chilling portrayal of the pre-teen tormentor
earned him two more Young Artist Award nominations.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.840
The kid's on a roll.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:46.840
Awake

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.240
Audiences definitely woke up when they first
saw Minnette spinning through the air in this

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:57.630
short-lived 2010 NBC police procedural. Starring
Jason Isaacs Awake followed an LAPD detective

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:02.030
who's torn between two different timelines
after a car accident launches him into the

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.030
supernatural.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:08.110
Minnette plays Britten's son, Rex, appearing
only in what's known as the "green reality,"

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:12.209
the world in which Rex survives the tragedy
and his mother doesn't. Apparently he has

00:02:12.209 --> 00:02:15.800
a gift for playing teens who may or may not
really exist...

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:16.800
Prisoners

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.440
In 2013, the then 17-year-old Minnette joined
an impressive ensemble in this thriller centered

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.689
around one father's primal reaction to an
unthinkable crime.

00:02:26.689 --> 00:02:31.519
Minnette plays Ralph Dover, son of Hugh Jackman's
Keller, who abducts and tortures a man he

00:02:31.519 --> 00:02:35.459
suspects has kidnapped his daughter. With
his fellow cast members, Minnette won the

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:39.219
National Board of Review Award for best ensemble.

00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:42.400
Alexander and the Terrible, Horrible, No Good,
Very Bad Day

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.109
Minnette's next project was a leading role
in this 2014 family comedy. Minnette played

00:02:47.109 --> 00:02:52.999
Alexander's older brother, Anthony, an accident-prone
teen dealing with the drama of an on-again/off-again

00:02:52.999 --> 00:02:56.890
relationship with his girlfriend, while also
struggling to pass his driving test ...

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:58.800
"I'll be your driving examiner."

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.020
"I don't think he passed."

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:08.140
Oops. But check out that Clay Jensen-esque
forehead bandage: How uncanny is that?

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.140
Goosebumps

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.930
Minnette jumped into the spooky world of R.
L. Stine in this 2015 comedy as Zach Cooper,

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:19.639
the fictionalized Stine's unassuming neighbor.
The film follows Zach as he settles into his

00:03:19.639 --> 00:03:24.519
new, small-town Maryland home after moving
from the Big Apple … and accidentally brings

00:03:24.519 --> 00:03:26.140
Stine's scary stories to life ...

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.200
"Maybe they're friendly?"

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:34.340
"Not friendly! Definitely not friendly!"

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.340
Don't Breathe

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:40.189
Minnette's most recent appearance on the silver
screen was in this claustrophobic 2016 horror

00:03:40.189 --> 00:03:45.279
gem as Alex, one of three friends who gets
trapped inside the house of a terrifying character

00:03:45.279 --> 00:03:49.719
known as "The Blind Man." Alex struggles to
make it out alive, facing multiple deadly

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.459
obstacles on his way.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:53.280
But that's not all...

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:58.840
Still don't know where you've seen Minnette?
How about his 2009 appearance as Danny Carter

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.310
in season four of Supernatural? Or as
a teen accused of murder on the supernatural

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:04.549
drama Medium?

00:04:04.549 --> 00:04:09.629
Or maybe his 2012 appearance on Law &amp; Order:
SVU as a troubled teen entangled in a sexual

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:14.469
assault case? What about his role as the icy
supervillain Blizzard on Marvel's Agents

00:04:14.469 --> 00:04:15.469
of S.H.I.E.L.D.?

00:04:15.469 --> 00:04:19.290
Or maybe you saw him get whacked on the heart-stopping
political drama Scandal, where he played the

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:22.130
president's doomed son? That'd be lucky 13.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:28.200
There you have it: thirteen reasons why Clay
from 13 Reasons Why looks so darn familiar.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.350
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:35.420
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

